bx is a mixed-license source tree.

bx-owned code
-------------
bx-owned code in this repository is available under the GNU General Public
License, version 2 or (at your option) any later version
("GPL-2.0-or-later"). The full GPLv2 text is included in COPYING.GPL-2.

Imported and upstream-derived code
----------------------------------
Copied or imported code keeps its original license and notices. Known upstream
areas include:

- src/applets/base/bc/ — BSD-2-Clause, plus extra third-party notices in some
  files
- src/applets/network/nc/netcat.[ch], socks.c — OpenBSD/BSD-style
  notices
- src/applets/network/traceroute/ — GPL-2.0-or-later
- src/applets/network/socat/ — includes code published under GPL version 2;
  see the file headers and COPYING.socat
- src/applets/system/init/ — BusyBox init-derived policy, GPL-2.0-or-later
- src/applets/text/awk/ — One True Awk (Lucent permissive license), with a
  public-domain Berkeley Yacc parser skeleton
- src/applets/text/sed/ — FreeBSD sed, BSD-3-Clause
- src/applets/text/ed/ — GNU ed, GPL-2.0-or-later
- src/applets/text/edit/vim/ — modified Vim, see src/applets/text/edit/COPYING.vim;
  the embedded xdiff library is LGPL-2.1-or-later (see COPYING.LGPL-2.1)
- src/applets/text/edit/runtime/ — curated Vim runtime subset; some files carry
  their own upstream notices
- src/vendor/jq/ — jq and bundled components, see src/vendor/jq/COPYING.
  The generated src/vendor/jq/src/parser.c and parser.h contain a Bison
  skeleton under GPL-3.0-or-later (COPYING.GPL-3) with the Bison special
  exception. The exception permits distributing this larger work under
  terms of our choice; bx is not a parser generator using the skeleton.
- src/lib/fetch/ — Mira-derived code under the MIT terms in
  src/lib/fetch/COPYING.Mira
- src/lib/manual/ — mandoc/OpenBSD-derived code under the terms collected in
  src/lib/manual/COPYING.mandoc
- src/applets/network/knock/ — GPL-2.0-or-later, derived from knock 0.8
- src/applets/network/rsync/ — ISC and other retained notices
- src/lib/fat/ and src/applets/system/fat/ — FreeBSD FAT utilities under
  BSD-2-Clause, with BSD-3-Clause checker diagnostics
- src/lib/zip/ — modified Info-ZIP code, not an official Info-ZIP release;
  see src/lib/zip/LICENSE.InfoZIP
- src/applets/archive/pigz/ — Zlib license

Subtree README/COPYING/LICENSE files and per-file headers control when they
differ from this top-level default.

Combined binary note
--------------------
bx is linked as one multicall executable. Because that combined work includes
components under different copyleft terms, the binary you ship must satisfy the
obligations of the included parts. The bx-owned grant is not a linking
exception for third-party code. Review the libraries in the actual build,
including archive members linked through dependencies. In particular, do not
distribute a GPLv2 binary incorporating legacy OpenSSL/SSLeay code under
its advertising terms without an applicable exception or other permission.

Distributors must also satisfy the corresponding-source requirements of
GPLv2 section 3 and the applicable LGPL terms. The license files installed
with bx do not replace the copyright notices in individual source files or
the notices required by linked libraries.
